### Create multiple widgets for testing

### Create Widget 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Basic Widget",
  "description": "A simple widget for basic tasks",
  "image": "basic-widget.jpg"
}

### Create Widget 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Advanced Widget",
  "description": "A more advanced widget with additional features",
  "image": "advanced-widget.jpg"
}

### Create Widget 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Premium Widget",
  "description": "Our top-of-the-line widget with all features",
  "image": "premium-widget.jpg"
}

### Get all widgets to verify creation
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets

### Update Widget 1 (replace 1 with actual ID after creation)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Basic Widget 2.0",
  "description": "An improved version of our basic widget",
  "image": "basic-widget-2.jpg"
}

### Get updated widget to verify changes
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets/1

### Search for widgets by name
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets?name=2.0

### Search for widgets by description
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets?description=advanced

### Search for widgets by both name and description
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/widgets?name=Widget&description=features
